ame yet however we can  reach an idea based on the debut trailer  many architectural and geographical  similarities to spain were noted  according to fans which makes this the  likely inspiration for scarlet and  violet the new starter names quaxly  sprigatito and fue coco also have  similarities to the spanish language now  in the first trailer we only saw the  three starters which of course fall into  the classic elemental trio of grass fire  and water now these typings have always  had this like rock paper scissors type  balance to them and they go all the way  back to the first game with game freak  leaving this mostly untouched personally  i get hyped the most when i see the  starters evolved forms however game  freak is still holding those cards  pretty close to their chest  we did however get to see some brand new  pokemon now we've got at least three  non-legendary new pokemon such as the  plant type smoliv the electric mouse  palmy because you know pokemon don't  have enough electric mouse pokemon  already right and the hilarious pig  leychonk not lebron not les mickey or  les salsa but le chunk it's real and he  looks and sounds kind of french too  it's a french pick yeah yeah you might  as well just end the video here he's  honestly perfect and in fact you know  what the legendaries i'm going off  script put late chunk on the cover or  give me some fan art of him at the  eiffel tower please make this happen  internet in all seriousness though le  chunk seems to be the standout for the  new pokemon revealed and according to  the official pokemon site lay chunk will  be used by your friend and rival named  mona you know speaking of the internet  when it comes to late chunk everyone's  been commenting on the tongue-in-cheek  references the game seems to be making  based on our slang after all referring  to lovable cats and dogs as being chunky  or even if you're cultured like me atomk  is basically an online pastime lei chunk  is more than welcome to the party  anecdotes aside we were able to catch a  glimpse of several other pokemon  returning for this region including the  classic fan favorites such as pikachu  meowth psyduck lucario and many others  curiously the trailer also showed the  hissuian variant of zoroark introduced  in pokemon legend's arceus now this is  cool because that opens the door up for  more history and variants but it is a  little confusing for me since those of  you who have played arceus will note  that the timeline of legends arceus is  largely different than that of the  modern pokemon games so it makes me  wonder were the events of legends arceus  namely the portal being open across  dimensions  did that have a reverse effect and  that's why we're seeing his informs in  the present day only time will tell  considering that there are hissuian  regional forms though this also opens  the door for gallerian forms and alolan  forms but we'll have to see in the  future what specifically will appear in  gen 9. lastly out of all the new pokemon  we've got the two legendaries corridon  and mariaden assuming that's how you  pronounce it and their design is pretty  sick the recurring theme seems to be  that of the past and the future are more  specifically tradition versus technology  and evolution it's an interesting  concept that is pretty apparent in the  design of the two legendary pokemon  karate and pokemon scarlet seem to be  representing the side of tradition while  at the same time marian and pokemon  violet have a more futuristic and  machine android style element to their  design you might have seen the trailer  and thought that there wasn't too much  that pushed the envelope forward  compared to prior gens still there are  some really intriguing features  according to the official site in the  trailers for starters it's going to be  an open world like seriously an actual  open world or more so than the past  games arceus was very close to this but  similarly to sword and shield it had  borders and loading screens between  towns which apparently won't be the case  here which sounds awesome according to  game freak various towns will blend  seamlessly into the wilderness without  borders you can see pokemon in the sky  seas forest streets and all over but  that's not all to help you explore this  new large open world gamefreak  introduces multiplayer you can play with  up to four players and explore which  okay has me seriously excited sword and  shield did have some fun multiplayer but  only in match made raid battles in  addition to the typical usual one-on-one  battling or trading features  unfortunately we don't know the nature  of the open world and how online  connectivity will properly work and i am  a little hesitant but cautiously  optimistic  i love pokemon and i grew up with the  series a lot so to be able to play with  my friends or colleagues that still play  yeah it's gonna be fun no matter what we  also get to meet some new characters one  of them is your friend nimona an  experienced trainer who will guide you  throughout your adventure and we also  meet the pokemon professors you have  professor sarah or professor turo and  for the first time they are version  exclusive they certainly look younger  and cooler than your typical professor  oak or rowan and one of them even  um kinda looks like  yeah  so i'm sure the overall plot of gen9  games will be no different than before  the professors will give you a pokedex  most likely and task you with traveling  all over the region to catch or see them  all and take on the pokemon league  so now you guys have to let me know how  you're feeling about the news so far are  y'all team sprightito like me what  regional variants do you hope to see and  how do we feel about professor chat i  mean professor turo  and which version are you guys gonna get  let me know in the comments below for  everything else pokemon stick with  gamespot until next time  [Music]  you
 

